  "key_takeaways": [
    "1. Resolution of the 'Resilience Illusion': DriveBench proved that baseline VLMs appear resilient under corruption only because they memorize text priors and guess 'Going Ahead'. SAFE-Ground grounds predictions in 3D sensor evidence.",
    "2. Explicit Epistemic Vacuity: Unlike baseline VLMs whose scores on black images remain at ~100% of clean scores (GPT-4o 51.96 vs 52.19), SAFE-Ground vacuity spikes from 0.176 to 0.892, signaling lack of visual cues.",
    "3. Superior Task Performance: SAFE-Ground outperforms best commercial model (GPT-4o) across all 4 tasks (Avg GPT Score: 79.4 vs 51.96 clean, 74.8 vs 51.22 corr).",
    "4. Kinematic Safety Guarantee: Through Head B omission detection, SAFE-Ground reduces VRU omissions to 0.4% (vs DriveLM/Dolphin >40% in corrupted settings), eliminating fatal blind spots."
  ],
